@stereotype(CIMStereotype.MCT)
@dataclass(repr=False, eq=False)
class ConductorPosition(SpacingPosition):
    '''
    Location of one or more conductors, together with the circuit they belong
    to, the kind of conductor they are meant to host, and a sequence number.
    The sequence number is used to match them with an ACLineSegmentPhase once
    the spacing is associated with an ACLineSegment. The position itself does
    not specify a phase.
    It is specialized by XYConductorPosition, for positions placed directly
    in an XYSpacing, and by SubConductorPosition, for conductors within a conductor
    group. For a SubConductorPosition, circuitNumber, kind and sequenceNumber
    may be left empty, in which case the value of the owning ConductorGroupPosition
    applies. That value is the sub-conductor's effective value.
    circuitNumber groups positions by circuit within the spacing, so a spacing
    kept as a library entry can describe several circuits before any ACLineSegment
    refers to it. Positions with the same sequenceNumber shall have the same
    circuitNumber. When the spacing is used, all positions with the same circuitNumber
    shall bind to ACLineSegmentPhases of the same ACLineSegment.
    '''

    circuitNumber: Optional[int] = field(
        default=None,
        metadata={
        'type': 'Attribute',
        'stereotypes': ['Attribute'],
        'minOccurs': '0',
        'maxOccurs': '1',
        'namespace': 'http://cim.ucaiug.io/cim101/draft#',
        'serialize': True,
        })
    '''
    Non-negative integer identifying the circuit the conductor(s) at this
    position belong to. It groups conductors by circuit within the spacing,
    so a spacing kept as a library entry can describe several circuits
    before it is associated with any ACLineSegment.
    Conductors shared by several circuits shall have circuitNumber 0. Examples
    are shield wires in multi-circuit transmission lines, shared neutrals
    in multi-circuit distribution lines, and the neutral messenger of an
    aerial bundled cable carrying more than one circuit.
    For a SubConductorPosition, if not specified, the circuitNumber of
    the owning ConductorGroupPosition applies. A ConductorGroupPosition
    whose sub-conductors belong to different circuits shall leave circuitNumber
    empty.
    Either every conductor in a spacing has an effective circuitNumber,
    or none does. When none does, all conductors belong to one circuit.
    Conductors with the same effective sequenceNumber shall have the same
    effective circuitNumber.
    When the spacing is associated with ACLineSegments, all conductors
    with the same non-zero circuitNumber shall correspond to ACLineSegmentPhases
    of the same ACLineSegment. Conductors with circuitNumber 0 correspond
    to one ACLineSegmentPhase in each ACLineSegment that shares them.
    '''
    
    sequenceNumber: Optional[int] = field(
        default=None,
        metadata={
        'type': 'Attribute',
        'stereotypes': ['Attribute'],
        'minOccurs': '0',
        'maxOccurs': '1',
        'namespace': 'http://cim.ucaiug.io/cim101/draft#',
        'serialize': True,
        })
    '''
    Number that links the conductor(s) at this position to the line segment
    that uses the spacing. The spacing itself does not assign a phase.
    When the spacing is associated with an ACLineSegment, the conductor(s)
    correspond to the ACLineSegmentPhase with the same sequenceNumber,
    and ACLineSegmentPhase.phase gives the phase.
    Conductors with the same effective sequenceNumber are meant to be connected
    in parallel: once the spacing is associated with an ACLineSegment,
    they correspond to the same ACLineSegmentPhase. This holds whether
    they are in the same group or elsewhere in the spacing.
    A conductor shared by several circuits (circuitNumber 0), such as a
    shared neutral or shield wire, corresponds to one ACLineSegmentPhase
    in each ACLineSegment that shares it. All of those ACLineSegmentPhases
    use this sequenceNumber.
    <b>Conductors without an effective sequenceNumber correspond to no
    ACLineSegmentPhase and are never considered parallel to one another.</b>
    Numbering implies no ordering between kinds: neutral and shield positions
    need not come after phase positions.
    For a SubConductorPosition, if not specified, the sequenceNumber of
    the owning ConductorGroupPosition applies. A ConductorGroupPosition
    whose sub-conductors are meant to be separate conductors (different
    sequence numbers) shall leave sequenceNumber empty. Examples are a
    trefoil formation, the cores of a multicore cable, and an aerial bundled
    cable.
    '''
    
    kind: Optional[ ConductorPositionKind ] = field(
        default=None,
        metadata={
        'type': 'Attribute',
        'stereotypes': ['enumeration', 'Attribute'],
        'minOccurs': '0',
        'maxOccurs': '1',
        'namespace': 'http://cim.ucaiug.io/cim101/draft#',
        'serialize': True,
        })
    '''
    Kind of conductor this position is meant to host, such as a phase conductor,
    a neutral, a shield wire or an earth conductor. It does not identify
    which phase; that is given only when the spacing is associated with
    an ACLineSegment.
    For a SubConductorPosition, if not specified, the kind of the owning
    ConductorGroupPosition applies. A ConductorGroupPosition whose sub-conductors
    are of different kinds shall use mixed, and each SubConductorPosition
    shall specify its own kind. The value mixed shall not be used for a
    WirePosition or a SubConductorPosition.
    '''
    
    @property
    def __namespace__(self):
        return 'http://cim.ucaiug.io/cim101/draft#'
    @property
    def __package__(self):
        return 'New Classes'
    @property
    def __minOccurs__(self):
        return '0'
    @property
    def __maxOccurs__(self):
        return 'unbounded'
    
